        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 家电",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "家电 — jiādiàn — \"household appliance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我们去年买了一些新家电 wǒmen qùnián mǎi le yìxiē xīn jiādiàn — We bought some new household appliances last year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "家电 (jiādiàn) is built from 家 'home' and 电 'electricity', both inherited from Middle Chinese, kae and denH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary explains the second as the flash when yin and yang clash, lightning; the sense 'electricity' is modern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
